WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.545
Separate a network prefix from host addresses with a /24.

00:00:05.545 --> 00:00:06.135
Yes.

00:00:06.135 --> 00:00:13.215
Both share the three octets covered by the 24-bit network prefix: 192.168.10.0/24.

00:00:14.215 --> 00:00:17.125
How many leading network bits does /24 describe?

00:00:17.125 --> 00:00:21.490
The number after the slash gives the number of leading prefix bits.
